-- title:
--   Regularity of the special fibre at ∞-branch cusps, q=2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=2$, let $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, algebraic over $\mathbb Q$, containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ for which there is a ring embedding $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota(\zeta)=e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L(\!(q)\!)$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_H(q^2M')$, where $H=\ker\big((\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times\big)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ such that $q$ lies in the maximal ideal, $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, and $\mathfrak m_A=(\varpi)$; assume $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j\in K$ be nonzero with $q$-expansion the image of $q^{-1}\cdot\mathrm{jNumQ}$, and let $\mathfrak X=\mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel}(A,K,j)$ be the scheme obtained by glueing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the integral closures of $A[j]$ and of $A[j^{-1}]$ in $K$ along the middle chart. Let $W_0\subseteq K$ be the valuation subring consisting of those $f$ for which there are power series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ nonzero modulo $\mathfrak m_A$ and $f\cdot y=x$ in $L(\!(q)\!)$. Let $z\in\mathfrak X$ and let $\varpi_z$ be the germ at $z$ of the global section obtained from $\varpi$ along the structure morphism $\mathfrak X\to\operatorname{Spec}A$; assume $\varpi_z$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk at $z$, that $z$ is not in the image of the finite chart $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the integral closure of $A[j]$, and that every prime $y$ of the chart algebra of $j^{-1}$ mapping to $z$ contains every element of that algebra whose image in $K$ is a non-unit of $W_0$. Then the quotient of the stalk of $\mathfrak X$ at $z$ by the ideal generated by $\varpi_z$ is a regular local ring.
--
--   This is the case $q=2$ of the regularity of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model of $X(\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M'))$ at the points of the Igusa branch through $\infty$ that are cusps, the branch being specified by the Gauss valuation ring $W_0$ of $A$-integral $q$-expansions. It is obtained from the corresponding statement for a point with localised chart data together with the production of a prime of the $j^{-1}$-chart containing $j^{-1}$ above $z$, and feeds the construction of a smooth open neighbourhood over $\operatorname{Spec}A$ and the stalkwise regularity statement at good points.
